---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ConfirmOfficial from "../components/ConfirmOfficial.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Where to live if you must stay"
  description="Andorra parishes compared for people who have to be in the country 90 or 183 days a year."
  path="/where-to-live"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Where to live if you must stay</h1>
    <p>
      Choose for light, height, the school run and the border you
      actually use. Do not choose from a winter photograph.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <ConfirmOfficial />
    <p>
      Companion to the live parish index,
      <a href="/parishes">The seven parishes</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Ninety days and 183 days are not the same life. A passive file
      can be a winter and a late summer. An active file is most of the
      year. If you cannot do the days, the parish does not matter.
    </p>
    <p>
      Official commune sites: Andorra la Vella, Escaldes-Engordany,
      Encamp, Canillo, Ordino, La Massana, Sant Julià de Lòria. We do
      not publish live asking prices on this page. Buying tax is on
      <a href="/buying-property">Buying property</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions that beat branding</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Where does the sun actually reach the street in January?</li>
      <li>How many steps, and what is the ice like on them?</li>
      <li>Who does the school run, and in which parish?</li>
      <li>Which border do you actually use — Spain or France?</li>
      <li>Can you get to Immigration, the bank and a supermarket without a performance?</li>
      <li>Does the building empty in May?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The seven parishes</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Parish</th>
          <th>If you have to stay</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Andorra la Vella</td>
          <td>
            The capital. Ministries, banks, the everyday centre of the
            valley. Urban without being metropolitan.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Escaldes-Engordany</td>
          <td>
            Joined to the capital. The public hospital, a broader
            residential grain, fewer of the capital’s busiest corners.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>La Massana</td>
          <td>
            Western valleys. Pal and Arinsal for ski; the village itself
            has a more year-round street.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Ordino</td>
          <td>
            Northern woodland and villages. Slower than the central
            valley. A short drive for larger errands.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Encamp</td>
          <td>
            Working parish on the road to Grandvalira. Pas de la Casa is
            a frontier ski-and-shop settlement, not everyday Andorra.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Canillo</td>
          <td>
            High eastern valley. Soldeu and El Tarter in winter. Further
            from the ministries. Confirm winter driving.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sant Julià de Lòria</td>
          <td>
            Southern gate on the Spanish road. Lower, less alpine,
            closer to Catalonia and the university.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      Related:
      <a href="/buying-property">Buying property</a>.
      We do not claim agencies on the
      <a href="/shortlist">shortlist</a>
      exist yet. Licensed agents with their own official sites are in
      the
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
